  <compounddef id="Safe-example" kind="example">
    <compoundname>Safe</compoundname>
    <briefdescription>
<para>nullptr handling </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>nullptr handling <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classcslt_1_1HeapAllocator" kindref="compound">cslt::HeapAllocator</ref><sp/>allocator;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">void</highlight><highlight class="normal">*<sp/>ptr<sp/>=<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">nullptr</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Safe<sp/>-<sp/>does<sp/>nothing</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">allocator.<ref refid="classcslt_1_1HeapAllocator_1aee2691eca10efc6a09848cfcdcec9c2c" kindref="member">return_element</ref>(ptr,<sp/>0,<sp/>0);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para>Always use the same alignment value that was used during allocation. Mismatched alignment can cause undefined behavior or crashes.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>Do not call return_element twice on the same pointer (double-free).</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>The bytes parameter is required by the interface but is not used by HeapAllocator since operator delete/free don&apos;t require size. <programlisting filename="Safe"></programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
